WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.817
Anyone can cook rasgulla at

2
00:00:01.817 --> 00:00:03.094
home. So what does a

3
00:00:03.094 --> 00:00:05.866
GI tag actually protect?

4
00:00:06.166 --> 00:00:07.989
A Geographical Indication says a

5
00:00:07.989 --> 00:00:09.568
product comes from a particular

6
00:00:09.568 --> 00:00:11.123
place, and owes its qualities

7
00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:11.716
to it.

8
00:00:11.716 --> 00:00:13.295
Darjeeling Tea was the first

9
00:00:13.295 --> 00:00:15.590
Indian product to get one.

10
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.678
India's GI law was passed

11
00:00:17.678 --> 00:00:18.978
in 1999,

12
00:00:18.978 --> 00:00:20.128
and came into force in

13
00:00:20.128 --> 00:00:22.063
2003.

14
00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:24.360
A registration lasts ten years,

15
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.260
and it can be renewed.

16
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.442
For prelims,

17
00:00:27.442 --> 00:00:29.219
link it to intellectual property

18
00:00:29.219 --> 00:00:31.587
and the WTO's TRIPS Agreement.

19
00:00:31.587 --> 00:00:32.678
It also ties in to

20
00:00:32.678 --> 00:00:35.566
rural livelihoods and exports.

21
00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:36.516
Your turn.

22
00:00:36.516 --> 00:00:37.549
How long is a GI

23
00:00:37.549 --> 00:00:39.438
registration valid?
